+++ b/desktop-android/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+# Original desktop darktable on Android (experimental)
+
+This separate APK packages the official **ARM64 darktable 5.6.2 desktop build**,
+including its original GTK widgets, data and modules. It does not reconstruct
+the editor in Compose, translate controls into HTML, or replace the pixelpipe.
+
+It is a **Linux/glibc compatibility runtime using PRoot**, with GTK3 Broadway
+rendering locally into WebView. It is **not a native Android/Bionic GTK port**.
+No remote desktop server, Termux installation, root access or CPU emulator is
+required on an ARM64 phone. QEMU is used only for Linux build-machine probes.
+
+## Scope and limits
+
+- All six original views are packaged: lighttable, darkroom, map, print,
+  slideshow and tethering. The official build enables OpenMP, OpenCL, Lua,
+  G'MIC, gPhoto2, OSMGpsMap, Colord and the original supported file formats.
+- Compiled support is not proof of Android integration. OpenCL drivers,
+  USB tethering, CUPS printing, MIDI, display ICC profiles and external editors
+  require platform support or additional bridges. Hardware parity is unverified.
+- The Android runtime has **not been executed on a physical device or Android
+  emulator** in the available environment. Linux/QEMU probes are not substitutes.
+- Android 8+ ARM64 is required. The launcher intentionally targets API 28:
+  PRoot must execute Linux ELF files from its private extracted filesystem.
+  Android's API 29+ writable-data execution restriction prevents simply raising
+  this target. This is a sideload experiment, not a Play Store release.
+- Allow at least 2 GB free storage for installation, runtime and initial data,
+  plus space for imported RAW copies, cache and exports.
+- This package has a separate application ID and separate catalog. The existing
+  mobile app is preserved. Do not migrate its development-5.8 databases or
+  version-7 masks into desktop 5.6.2; backwards compatibility is not established.
+
+## Working with photos
+
+1. Start the app and wait for verified runtime extraction and original GTK startup.
+2. Android **Import** copies selected files into private `/photos`. Open that
+   folder with darktable's original import dialog. Provider originals are intact.
+3. Work in the original desktop panels. Landscape orientation, pinch zoom and
+   a physical keyboard/mouse are useful; the Android keyboard button is available.
+4. Export with darktable's original panel into `/exports` (the default adaptation).
+   Android **Export** then saves a selected result through the system file picker.
+5. Use **Session** to stop/restart the runtime. Runtime files and photo/catalog
+   state are stored separately. Stopping the service forcibly ends the session;
+   close darktable normally before stopping when practical.
+
+## Build
+
+Use JDK 17, Gradle 8.14.4, Android SDK 35/build-tools 35.0.0. Build the runtime
+outside the repository; do not commit extracted files or APKs to source Git.
+
+Prepare a Debian trixie ARM64 root filesystem (official `arm64v8/debian:trixie-slim`)
+with configured APT packages `libgtk-3-bin fonts-dejavu-core libgomp1 libasound2t64
+libgpg-error0 libgcrypt20 tzdata dbus-daemon dbus-bin libglx0 libgl1 libegl1
+iso-codes libx11-xcb1 libdrm2 libxcb-dri3-0 libgbm1 libusb-1.0-0`. Retain package copyright
+files and dpkg metadata. Unpack the verified official ARM64 AppImage with
+`unsquashfs -o 936456 -d APPDIR Darktable-5.6.2-aarch64.AppImage`.
+
+Extract the verified Termux `proot`, `libtalloc` and `libandroid-shmem` ARM64
+packages into a separate prefix. See [SOURCES.md](SOURCES.md) for versions and hashes.
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/assemble-runtime.py \
+  --rootfs /absolute/rootfs --appimage /absolute/Darktable-5.6.2-aarch64.AppImage \
+  --appdir /absolute/APPDIR --termux-prefix /absolute/termux/usr \
+  --output /absolute/new-stage
+gradle -PdesktopRuntimeStage=/absolute/new-stage \
+  :app:testDebugUnitTest :app:testReleaseUnitTest :app:assembleRelease :app:lintRelease
+python3 tools/verify-apk.py app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk \
+  --stage /absolute/new-stage --report /absolute/apk-verification.json
+```
+
+The packager requires a fresh output path, checks the official AppImage digest,
+retains original file bytes, creates an inventory, and excludes build-machine
+IPC, caches, test photos and user homes. The installer checks the complete payload
+SHA-256 and safely extracts USTAR entries without following directory symlinks.
+The release build currently uses Gradle's development signing key.
+
+For Java-only checks, without packaging a falsely empty APK:
+
+```sh
+gradle -PdesktopSourceChecksOnly=true :app:testDebugUnitTest :app:testReleaseUnitTest
+```
+
+The display HTTP endpoint requires a random session cookie. GTK's upstream HTTP
+socket stays in the private filesystem; its native socket uses a random runtime
+directory. No JavaScript-to-Java bridge or WebView file access is exposed.
+PRoot is a compatibility tool, **not a security sandbox**.
